  <iati-identifier>GB-GOV-1-301457-432</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="GB-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK - Foreign, Commonwealth Development Office (FCDO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Demand for Merit Based Recruitment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project focuses on one of the most pressing fields in Montenegro: public sector recruitment. With the effort of mapping the risks of undue politicisation and corruption during recruitment already conducted, the project will further promote the findings and the recommendations stemming from this pioneering endeavour. It will also ensure new perspectives in this important field, by ensuring continuous monitoring of public sector recruitment procedures, which will result in a number of citizen-facing, public outreach and advocacy activities, which will be largely aligned with the citizens&#x2019; concerns, on one hand, and with the Government&#x2019;s and Parliament&#x2019;s policy agendas, on the other. The main impact of the project is to increase evidence-based public demand for merit-based recruitment practices across the Montenegrin public sector, and thus, in the long-term contribute to more meritocratic procedures and practices.</narrative>
  </description>
